From: Allan Siriani <allan@fatecpompeia.edu.br>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: wcn36xx: don't dereference a missing band on 2.4 GHz-only chips

The WCN3620 only registers the 2.4 GHz band, but during scans the firmware
reports some frames as 5 GHz. wcn36xx_update_survey() then dereferences a
NULL sband inside the IRQ handler and the whole SoC hard-locks until the
watchdog resets it (about 3 minutes after Wi-Fi comes up).

- wcn36xx_update_survey(): return if the band is not registered (same idea
  as the fix posted to linux-wireless in October 2026);
- wcn36xx_rx_skb(): drop frames for bands the wiphy does not have, so
  mac80211 does not WARN on them either.

Tested on the Motorola Moto G 2013 (falcon, WCN3620), Linux 6.16.

diff -ruN a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/txrx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/txrx.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/txrx.c	2026-11-02 22:36:37.827477244 -0300
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/txrx.c	2026-11-02 22:36:37.838477489 -0300
@@ -286,6 +286,10 @@
 		idx = wcn->hw->wiphy->bands[NL80211_BAND_2GHZ]->n_channels;
 
 	sband = wcn->hw->wiphy->bands[band];
+	/* WCN3620 only registers 2.4 GHz; scan metadata may still say 5 GHz */
+	if (!sband)
+		return;
+
 	channel = sband->channels;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < sband->n_channels; i++, channel++) {
@@ -295,6 +299,9 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+	if (i == sband->n_channels)
+		return;
+
 	spin_lock(&wcn->survey_lock);
 	wcn->chan_survey[idx].rssi = rssi;
 	wcn->chan_survey[idx].snr = snr;
@@ -380,6 +387,11 @@
 		status.freq = WCN36XX_CENTER_FREQ(wcn);
 	}
 
+	/* WCN3620 only registers 2.4 GHz: drop scan frames tagged as 5 GHz
+	 * here (otherwise mac80211 WARNs with a stack trace for each one) */
+	if (!wcn->hw->wiphy->bands[status.band])
+		goto drop;
+
 	wcn36xx_update_survey(wcn, status.signal, get_snr(bd),
 			      status.band, status.freq);
 
